                "reviews": [
                    {
                        "recommendationid": "236735075",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561197988764422",
                            "num_reviews": 8,
                            "playtime_forever": 5569,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0,
                            "playtime_at_review": 5569,
                            "last_played": 1790895333
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I had read some of the reviewres points. Some are fair, while I disagree with others.\n\n[H3]Positives:[/H3]\n[B]The Visual design[/B] is GREAT one if not the strongest point of the game, from the buildings to the propaganda and industruial security posters. the devs even gave us translations to most of the signals, posters and other visual elements which was a nice touch for those of us that dont speak russian.\n[B]It runs well[/B] I was doubting about buying it because I thought It would run slowly on my system, but nope.\n\n[H3]Negatives:[/H3]\n[B]Combat and Combat mechanics[/B] Things changes a lot through the main game and the DLC. It felt to me like there was either no coherence or they are experimenting a lot with it.\n[B]Differences among the open and closed areas[/B] UGH the infinite respawn enemies. When you need to watch some \"X things that I hope I know before\" youtube videos to have a better grasp about the game, then your game design is lacking.\n\n[H3](Some)Things that I disegree with other reviewers:[/H3]\n[B]Characters being hard / unlikable / insufferable[/B] Well, this is a game developed in another country, and it is spected to have some cultural differences. I liked that, why? I want a game that reflects the \"what if\" but from another perpective.\n[B]Music[/B] There is told in several places that one of the technologies developed was the \"radio from the future\", that allows to hear comms from the future, among those are music. if you pay attention you see a VOV-A playing a remix from a russian song on a keyboard in the intro, that should be enough to set up some expetatives. I get it some poeple expected a blast from the past soundtrack like in fallout or even Bioshock, but remember, even Bioshock played with \"music fom the future\" concept in Infinite.´\n[B]Too much cussing[/B]: I for one f***ing love it! I dont expect that in a disaster FUBAR-like scenario every character is to be expected to perfectly following pre-disaster social norms.\n[B]Unlikable MC[/B] I did like how he starts like a loyal indoctrinated soldier and how that gets changes as the story progresses. But  yeah some things could be fleshed out more.\n[B]Unlikable characters[/B] Well, the mails and interactions let us see how some of people in power are jerks, who would had guessed that huh? So yeah, those are represented well\n\n[H3]Conclusions:[/H3]\nWhile this game is not perfect, I appreciate the vision they had and the ambition to give us something infused with a different perpective. Yes they tried a lot of things,  and some didt land, as is to be expected from a new gamedev. While I dont liked some of the experiments, I liked that they have the initiiative to try them out. \nAnd, please lets not forget, in 3 and a half years (since launch), or 8 (since the official trailer in 2018) they gave us way more content, better frames per second numbers, less loading screens, and less bugs than others developers with hundreds if not thousands of employees did. Food for tought me thinks.",
